  "result": "The reviewer agent is now read-only. I changed `.claude/agents/reviewer.md` in three ways:\n\n- **Removed `Edit`** from `tools`, so it only has `Read, Grep, Glob`.\n- **Removed `memory: project`.** Memory automatically gives the agent Read, Write and Edit so it can manage its memory files, which meant it could still write files even without `Edit` in its list.\n- **Added `disallowedTools: Edit, Write, NotebookEdit, Bash`.** This blocks writes even if someone adds these tools back to `tools` later. Bash is on the list because shell commands like `sed -i` or `>` can change files.\n\nOne thing you lose: the reviewer no longer keeps project memory between runs. If you want that back, the agent would need write access, at least to its own memory folder.\n\nI didn't run `npm run lint` or `npm run build` because this only changes agent config, not app code.",
